    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A midland Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#saxons">Saxon</a> kingdom that grew from a frontier people into the largest and strongest of the English kingdoms.</li><li>Under Æthelbald and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#offa-of-mercia">Offa</a> (716–796) it dominated southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#england">England</a>, built Offa's Dyke and dealt with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#wessex">Wessex</a> broke its power in 825; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#vikings">Vikings</a> split it in 877, and western Mercia joined the English kingdom in 918.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#offa-of-mercia">Offa</a> issued a gold coin copying an Abbasid dinar, complete with an Arabic inscription, to which the moneyer added the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#latin">Latin</a> words OFFA REX.</p></aside>
    </section>

